{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "reason": "React-only entrypoints: the package root is the React entry and /catalog holds the framework-free definitions. Rebaselined 2026-11-06 after 32 more Lumi UI components (overlays, media, display, choice and tree controls), the Admin connected components and the redesigned Upload and charts landed; the growth is Lumi-owned component code with dependencies kept external, and maxima allow about 5% growth. Rebaselined again 2026-11-07 after the component gap work landed: CodeBlock and CodeEditor (only their shells; the grammars and CodeMirror stay in the lazy chunks below), ten Agent UI components with framework-free message schemas (re-exported from /catalog, hence ui-catalog-js), Empty, ActivityFeed, the funnel chart, ColorSwatches, the ImageGrid uploader and calendar month/year panels, plus their styles in ui-css; admin-entry-js also carries the demo's component overview thumbnails and rebuilt Developer pages. Baselines are the measured sizes and the raised maxima again allow about 5% growth. ui-shared-js is the code the root and the charts entry share: the UI text context, cn, the bundled icon map with its lazy full-set loader, and the Empty state the charts draw when there is no data (moved out of the root, not added). The full HugeIcons set is a lazy chunk of its own (admin-icons-js), loaded only for names outside the bundled icon map. Code highlighting and the code editor are lazy chunks too: *-code-highlight-js holds the Lezer grammars and the shared tag map CodeBlock loads on first render, *-code-editor-js holds CodeMirror and imports the highlighter statically so the two never split into a third shared chunk; that static import is why rolldown gives the root's dynamic import a re-export facade (ui-code-highlight-entry-js). Rebaselined 2026-11-08 after the Prose, Markdown and Html content components, the Article page, the numbered Pagination variant and the content styles landed; DOMPurify stays an external dependency of the UI package and the Admin app loads it as a lazy chunk of its own (admin-html-sanitizer-js) on the first Html block. Rebaselined 2026-11-10 after the data layer parity work: tenants, live updates, optimistic and undoable writes, CanAccess, URL-synced lists, CSV/JSON import and export, document titles and the audit log with its activity-feed view grow admin-entry-js (the demo also gains import/export buttons and a change history section); ui-js and ui-css grow by the Agent prompt input and message refinements. Baselines are the measured sizes and the maxima keep their previous headroom. Rebaselined again 2026-11-10 after code grammars became per-language chunks: the highlighter and the editor keep only JSON, every other language loads through its own import() (grammar-* for CodeBlock, language-* for CodeMirror, which re-exports the matching grammar chunk so the two never split a shared Lezer chunk), so a JSON-only page loads the highlighter at about a fifth of its former size. The highlight and editor chunks now hold those dynamic imports, hence their dynamic capabilities; code-* chunks in the UI dist are the re-export facades rolldown gives a dynamic import whose chunk is also imported statically. Existing maxima stayed or shrank; the new entries carry the measured sizes with about 5% (at least a few hundred bytes) headroom.",
